# REQUIRES: verilator
# Fixes for an FSD 1,024-node fold whose controls, token channels and resets
# crossed the device (a32-F4, 11-12).
# --slr-group-control: each class's controls (its sequencer, from its own next
# position of its parent's; its bubble register; its slot tables and their
# register chains) built in its class's SLR group, not in the simulator level.
# The same netlist but for the hierarchy: it matches the target in exactly the
# host cycles of the fold without the option (nested sequencers, bubbles,
# stalls). --slr-group-reset: the reset registered once in each group and once
# for the level; the simulator leaves reset a host cycle later (one host cycle
# more), its handshakes held low in that host cycle (the testbench offers a
# token the host cycle after its reset falls: without the hold the first token
# is lost and the run times out).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/late
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/base --static --nest --bubbles --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-count 3 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/base/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/base/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/base/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/base/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=30 +bubble=30 +burst=4 | grep MATCH > %t/base/r1.txt
# RUN: %t/base/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=0 +bubble=0 | grep MATCH > %t/base/r2.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/base/r1.txt
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/ctl --static --nest --bubbles --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-count 3 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-group-control --slr-level 2 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CTL < %t/ctl/foldsim_sim.sv
# --slr-level 2: the floorplan puts the level's cells (the simulator's but its
# groups) and the environment beside it with group 2.
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEVEL < %t/ctl/foldsim_floorplan.tcl
# LEVEL: set c [get_cells -quiet -hierarchical foldsim_slr0]
# LEVEL: # The simulator level and its environment with group 2 (--slr-level).
# LEVEL-NEXT: set g [get_cells -quiet -hierarchical foldsim_slr2]
# LEVEL: set c [get_cells -quiet -filter {NAME !~ "*/foldsim_slr*"} $sim/*]
# LEVEL-NEXT: if {[llength $c] > 0} { set_property USER_SLR_ASSIGNMENT fs_slr2 $c }
# LEVEL: /env]
# LEVEL-NEXT: if {[llength $e] == 1} { set_property USER_SLR_ASSIGNMENT fs_slr2 $e }
# Without --slr-level: no level lines.
# RUN: not grep -q 'slr-level' %t/base/foldsim_floorplan.tcl
# CTL-LABEL: module foldsim_sim_slr0(
# CTL: Leaf_seq
# CTL: Leaf_bubble
# CTL: Leaf_state2
# CTL-LABEL: module foldsim_sim_slr1(
# CTL: Leaf_copy1_seq
# CTL: Leaf_copy1_bubble
# CTL: Leaf_copy2_seq
# CTL: Leaf_copy2_bubble
# CTL-LABEL: module foldsim_sim(
# CTL-NOT: Leaf{{(_copy[12])?}}_seq <=
# CTL-NOT: Leaf{{(_copy[12])?}}_bubble <=
# CTL: endmodule
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/ctl/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/ctl/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/ctl/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/ctl/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=30 +bubble=30 +burst=4 | grep MATCH > %t/ctl/r1.txt
# RUN: %t/ctl/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=0 +bubble=0 | grep MATCH > %t/ctl/r2.txt
# RUN: diff %t/base/r1.txt %t/ctl/r1.txt
# RUN: diff %t/base/r2.txt %t/ctl/r2.txt
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/rst --static --nest --bubbles --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-count 3 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-group-control --slr-group-reset Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RST < %t/rst/foldsim_sim.sv
# RST-LABEL: module foldsim_sim_slr0(
# RST: reset_slr0 <= hostReset;
# RST-LABEL: module foldsim_sim_slr1(
# RST: reset_slr1 <= hostReset;
# RST-LABEL: module foldsim_sim(
# RST: reset_level <= hostReset;
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/rst/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/rst/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/rst/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/rst/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=30 +bubble=30 +burst=4 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/rst/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=0 +bubble=0 | grep MATCH > %t/rst/r2.txt
# RUN: python3 -c "import re,sys; h=lambda f: int(re.search(r'in (\d+) host', open(f).read()).group(1)); a, b = h(sys.argv[1]), h(sys.argv[2]); print('HOST', b - a)" %t/base/r2.txt %t/rst/r2.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLUS1
# PLUS1: HOST 1
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
# --slr-group-local: each group computes the level's logic it reads (the
# frame decision's go and advance, a frame input's select) from their
# registers, so every value entering a group leaves a register
# (foldsim_xcheck.py: 0 edges with logic; without the option the decision's
# go / advance cross as logic). The same MATCH and host cycles.
# RUN: not python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_xcheck.py %t/ctl/foldsim_sim.mlir | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=XBASE
# XBASE: cross-group edges: {{.*}}LOGIC {{[1-9]}}
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/loc --static --nest --bubbles --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-count 3 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-group-control --slr-group-local 1000 Leaf > %t/loc.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOCLOG < %t/loc.log
# LOCLOG: slr-group-local: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} level ops cloned into groups, 0 cones left in the level
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_xcheck.py %t/loc/foldsim_sim.mlir | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=XLOC
# XLOC: cross-group edges: {{.*}} LOGIC 0 (0 bits); group outputs read by the level: {{[0-9]+}}, LOGIC 0
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/loc/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/loc/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/loc/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/loc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=30 +bubble=30 +burst=4 | grep MATCH > %t/loc/r1.txt
# RUN: %t/loc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=0 +bubble=0 | grep MATCH > %t/loc/r2.txt
# RUN: diff %t/base/r1.txt %t/loc/r1.txt
# RUN: diff %t/base/r2.txt %t/loc/r2.txt
# --slr-group-own: each group owns the level's control it reads (S26 concept
# A, a32-S26X 11-14): the level registers a group reads (the sequencer's
# positions, the token counters, a link's held bit) replicated into the group
# with their next-value cones. foldsim_locality.py: without it the level's
# pos0 / token counters fan out over the SLRs through logic (L3 REFUSE); with
# it no level register spans the groups (the kernel beside group 2). The same
# MATCH and host cycles.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/own --static --nest --bubbles --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-region v80 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-group-control --slr-group-reset --slr-level 2 --slr-group-local 1000 --slr-group-own 1000 Leaf > %t/own.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OWNLOG < %t/own.log
# OWNLOG: slr-group-own: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} level registers and {{[0-9]+}} level ops replicated into groups, 0 closures left
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/own0 --static --nest --bubbles --copies Leaf:3 --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --slr-groups --slr-region v80 --slr-assign Leaf:0,Leaf_copy1:1,Leaf_copy2:1,Top_model:2 --slr-group-control --slr-group-reset --slr-level 2 --slr-group-local 1000 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: not python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_locality.py %t/own0 --out %t/own0/l --kernel-slr SLR0 > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OWN0 < %t/own0/l/locality.txt
# OWN0: REFUSE control   %pos0
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_locality.py %t/own --out %t/own/l --kernel-slr SLR0 > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OWN < %t/own/l/locality.txt
# A class whose parent sits in another group loads posD's next position
# (every sequencer holds posD's value), its group's own: no other group's
# sequencer enters a group.
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OWNSEQ < %t/own/foldsim_sim.sv
# OWNSEQ-LABEL: module foldsim_sim_slr0(
# OWNSEQ-NOT: _seq,
# OWNSEQ: );
# OWN: L3 global fanout
# OWN-NOT: REFUSE
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/own/obj %S/Inputs/tb_late.sv top.sv %t/own/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/own/build.log 2>&1
